{"id":"000W3T","title":"Balanced X-Sums","author":"Ambrose","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-18T22:03:45+00:00","posted":"Heute, 18:25 Uhr","rules":"Inspired by the impressive series of balanced sudokus by Nell Gwyn, check them out!\n\nRules\n\nBalanced Latin Square: Place an integer from {−3,−2,−1,0,1,2,3} in each cell so that each integer appears exactly once in each row and column.\n\nDirected X-Sums: For a clue outside the grid, let X be the number in the cell closest to it. If X=0, the clue must be 0. If X is positive, the clue equals the sum of the values in the first X cells in that row/column starting at the cell next to the clue. If X is negative, the clue equals the sum of the first |X| cells in that row/column starting from the opposite end from the clue.\n\nSolve Online: Sudokupad","solutionCode":"Rows 3 and 5 in absolute value, Western reading order.","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/xnp25xu6ua","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/xnp25xu6ua","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":7,"cols":7,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-18T22:03:45+00:00"}